@startuml c4-runner-code
!pragma layout smetana
!include theme.iuml
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title C4 Level 4: notebook runner code dependencies
class "run-practice-labs.py" as Runner <<module>> {
  main()
}
class "argparse.ArgumentParser" as Parser <<stdlib>> {
  add_argument()
  parse_args()
  error()
}
class "pathlib.Path" as Path <<stdlib>> {
  glob()
  rglob()
  mkdir()
}
class "nbformat" as Format <<library module>> {
  read(source, as_version=4)
  write(notebook, target)
}
class "nbclient.NotebookClient" as Client <<library class>> {
  execute()
}
class "nbformat.NotebookNode" as Node <<library data object>> {
  metadata
  cells
}
Runner --> Parser : parses and validates selection options
Runner --> Path : discovers sources and creates result paths
Runner --> Format : reads sources; saves copies in finally
Runner --> Client : constructs with timeout, kernel and working directory
Format --> Node : read() returns notebook
Client --> Node : executes and updates cell outputs
note bottom of Runner
  main() returns 0 for list mode or complete success.
  main() returns 1 after an execution error.
  The __main__ guard calls sys.exit(main()).
  There are no separate discovery/execution service classes.
end note
note bottom of Client
  allow_errors=False
  Working directory = source.parent
  Non-Python kernel metadata is preserved.
end note
legend bottom
  Focus: the notebook acceptance runner component from Level 3.
  Library interfaces are shown only where used by this repository's code.
  This is a code dependency view, not a claim to model nbclient internals.
endlegend
@enduml
